/given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Dates from the molecular clock: how wrong can we be?</article-title><source>Trends Ecol Evol</source><volume>22</volume><fpage>180</fpage><lpage>184</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17157408</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b49-ebo-4-075"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rambaut</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Bromham</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Estimating divergence dates from molecular sequences</article-title><source>Mol Biol Evol</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>442</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9549094</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b50-ebo-4-075"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rannala</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Yang</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Inferring speciation times under an episodic molecular clock</article-title><source>Syst Biol</source><volume>56</volume><fpage>453</fpage><lpage>66</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17558967</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b51-ebo-4-075"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Renner</surname><given-names>SS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Relaxed molecular clocks for dating historical plant dispersal events</article-title><source>Trends Plant Sci</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>550</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16226053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b52-ebo-4-075"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rodr&#x000ed;guez-Trelles</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Tarr&#x000ed;o</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ayala</surnam